          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तारो (tāro) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from tārā, \"fixed star\". CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry (CDIAL 5798); the match is through Hindi tārā and Gujarati tāro. English star is a distant cousin."
            }
